.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-aep - AceTeam Execution Proof receipt tools


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel aep [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Tools for working with signed AEP (AceTeam Execution Proof) receipts.

.PP
An AEP receipt is the signed grounding/trust proof a Citadel node attaches to
an inference job's output. \fBcitadel aep verify\fR checks its ECDSA signature
offline against a node's public identity.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for aep


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--node-dir\fP=""
	Override the node config directory (citadel.yaml + services/), bypassing $HOME/ConfigDir resolution. Also settable via CITADEL_NODE_DIR. Scope: manifest/services resolution only -- does NOT redirect network state, the module lockfile, or nodevault.

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel(1)\fP, \fBcitadel-aep-verify(1)\fP
